## What the correction establishes

The existing real open operands were projected with every base/addition identifier and
class, both weights, loss and tolerance preserved. No joint reference world was introduced.
The current Engine and the corrected Fable producer both retain [-8,8]; the plan reports
`no_admitted_reference`, no question depth and no ambiguity witness. This is the right
description of the missing prerequisite, not a new physical result.

Three honest constructed controls also pass: the missing-reference case, the adaptive
depth-two/fixed-set-three case, and the two-world geometry ambiguity. Fable's 34 focused
planner/checker tests pass in a private reconstruction of the selected source. These are
scoped software checks, not external scientific review or evidence of reviewer effort.
The planner and its checker share the cohort producer's enclosure and matching calculation;
their search procedures differ. This review does not establish independent matching evidence.
The Engine candidate's 93 measurement tests and research consistency check also pass.

